  "title": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: Fix memory leaks and changeTime overflow bug",
  "description": "Fix changeTime millisecond calculation that used a single subtraction\ninstead of proper modular arithmetic. If start_ms + ms exceeded 2000,\nthe old code would leave an invalid millisecond value (>= 1000). Also\nfix the off-by-one (> 1000 should be >= 1000). Replace with:\n  second += elapsed_ms / 1000;\n  elapsed_ms = elapsed_ms % 1000;\n\nFix three memory leaks in file_open:\n- str_fileformatversion was never freed (both match and mismatch paths)\n- xmlFreeDoc(doc) was missing when fileFormatVersion != \"32.423\"\n- xmlFreeDoc(doc) was missing on the success path (WTAP_OPEN_MINE),\n  leaking the entire parsed XML document for the file's lifetime\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Kiro)",
